        "original_id": "eceed6e0-f1e5-59b7-b87f-03ac2a7998cd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Conrad, Gregory \"Pappy\" Boyington, Sam Waterston, David Soul, Frank M. Robinson, Thomas N. Scortia\n- Products: Baa Baa Black Sheep, Black Sheep Squadron, The Fifth Missile, The Gold Crew\n- Roles: American combat pilot, United States Marine Corps fighter ace\n- Topics: World War II, television series, TV movies, ballistic missile submarines\n\nFacts:\n- Gregory \"Pappy\" Boyington was born on December 4, 1912, and he became an American combat pilot and a United States Marine Corps fighter ace during World War II.\n- Robert Conrad portrayed World War II ace Pappy Boyington in the television series \"Baa Baa Black Sheep,\" which was later syndicated as \"Black Sheep Squadron.\"\n- The 1986 TV movie \"The Fifth Missile\" starred Robert Conrad, Sam Waterston, and David Soul.\n- \"The Fifth Missile\" is about an American ballistic missile submarine.\n- \"The Fifth Missile\" was based on the novel \"The Gold Crew\" by Frank M. Robinson and Thomas N. Scortia.\n- Gregory \"Pappy\" Boyington died on January 11, 1988.",
